Article 20
(1) In the implementation of protection services for women, the Regional Government establishes P2TP2A as a service network for women victims of violence.
(2) The establishment of P2TP2A is intended so that women victims of violence obtain comprehensive, integrated, quality, inclusive and sustainable services.
(3) P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) has the following duties:
a. provide services to women victims of violence in accordance with standard operating procedures; b. coordinate prevention, services and referrals between government-owned service institutions, community-owned service institutions, professional organizations, law enforcement institutions and other related institutions;
c. conduct data collection on case services;
d. provide various information needed by victims, victims' families and the community;
e. conduct prevention of recurrence of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women; f. conduct monitoring and evaluation of victim services; and
g. provide capacity strengthening, guidance and assistance related to victim services.

Article 23
(1) Services are implemented to fulfill the rights of women victims of violence and are carried out with the following principles:
a. respect for human rights; b. non-discrimination;
c. confidentiality;
d. empathy;
e. inclusion;
f. empowerment;
g. victim-based decisions;
h. honesty;
i. professionalism;
j. integration; and
k. sustainability.
(2) Services to women victims of violence must consider special conditions and needs based on the vulnerabilities experienced by women as referred to in Article 20

REGENT OF MAMUJU
WEST SULAWESI PROVINCE
REGIONAL REGULATION OF MAMUJU REGENCY
NUMBER 9 YEAR 2023
CONCERNING
EMPOWERMENT AND PROTECTION OF WOMEN
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF MAMUJU,

Considering : a. that the fulfillment of constitutional rights and protection of women's human rights regarding empowerment and protection of women is one of the values contained in Pancasila and the 1945 Constitution;
b. that women play a very important role in the process of continuation and creation of quality generations, thus requiring a sense of security, obtaining guarantees of protection from acts of violence and discrimination, and need to be empowered in order to actualize their potential optimally;
c. that based on Law Number 23 Year 2014 concerning Regional Government as mentioned in the Appendix, it is stated that the division of government affairs in the field of women's empowerment with one of the sub-affairs is the protection of women;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Empowerment and Protection of Women;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 29 Year 1959 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions in Sulawesi (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1959 Number 74, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1822);
3. Law Number 23 Year 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 6 Year 2023 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 Year 2022 concerning Job Creation into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2023 Number 41, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6856);
4. Law Number 12 Year 2022 concerning Criminal Acts of Sexual Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2022 Number 120, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6792);

With the Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF MAMUJU REGENCY and

